<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern African Customs Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1910</span> · Also known as SACU</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/customs-union">Customs Union</a>, established in 1910 with the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, is the oldest existing customs union in the world. Its members are South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, Lesotho, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>, which share a common external tariff and divide the pooled customs revenue by a formula. These revenues form a large part of the budgets of the smaller members.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southern-african-customs-union.jpg" alt="Southern African Customs Union" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BlankMap-Africa.svg: Lokal_Profil derivative work: Htonl (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southern_African_Customs_Union.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
